{"schemaVersion":1,"sourceRecord":{"schemaVersion":1,"recordId":"wikibooks-446399-r4514047","sourceId":"wikibooks-cookbook-cc-by-sa","sourceTitle":"Cookbook:Beef and Gizzard Sauce","sourcePageId":446399,"sourceRevision":"4514047","sourceRevisionTimestamp":"2025-06-19T01:42:49Z","sourceRevisionUser":"Kittycataclysm","sourceUrl":"https://en.wikibooks.org/w/index.php?title=Cookbook:Beef%20and%20Gizzard%20Sauce&oldid=4514047","retrievedAt":"2026-10-13T12:24:42.134Z","sourceCategories":["Category:Easy recipes","Category:Recipes","Category:Recipes using beef flank"],"license":{"id":"wikibooks-cookbook-cc-by-sa-4.0","name":"Creative Commons Attribution-ShareAlike 4.0 International (CC BY-SA 4.0); Wikibooks text is generally dual-licensed with GFDL unless otherwise noted","evidenceUrl":"https://en.wikibooks.org/wiki/Wikibooks:Copyrights","policyStatus":"verified-license","pageExceptionStatus":"not-reviewed-per-page","attribution":"Attribute Wikibooks contributors by linking each version-specific source page. Indicate that structured fields are extracted and any translated or edited text is modified. Include CC BY-SA 4.0 notice/link and share adaptations under CC BY-SA 4.0 or later.","changeNoticeRequired":true,"shareAlikeRequired":true},"sourceSha256":"f043a9b79747eb6db4b629025c293b48cd6312459b85fcfd943147b866595e6e","sourceWikitext":"__NOTOC__\n{{Recipe summary\n| Category = Beef recipes\n| Difficulty = 2\n}}\n\n{{Recipe}}\n\n'''Beef and gizzard sauce''' is a Nigerian beef dish typically eaten with white rice, spaghetti, fried plantain, or boiled yam.\n\n==Ingredients==\n* 1 [[Cookbook:Kilogram|kg]] [[Cookbook:Chicken|chicken]] gizzard, washed\n* 1 [[Cookbook:Tablespoon|tablespoon]] [[Cookbook:Salt|salt]]\n* 1 small [[Cookbook:Onion|onion]], [[Cookbook:Dice|diced]]\n* 2 beef [[Cookbook:Bouillon Cube|stock cubes]]\n* 1 tablespoon [[Cookbook:Curry Powder|curry powder]]\n* 1 tablespoon [[Cookbook:Thyme|thyme]]\n* 1 kg [[Cookbook:Beef|beef]] flank steak, cut in bite-sized pieces\n* 1 medium onion, [[Cookbook:Chopping|chopped]]\n* 2 beef stock cubes\n* 1 tablespoon thyme\n* 1 tablespoon curry powder\n* 1 tablespoon salt\n* [[Cookbook:Vegetable oil|Vegetable oil]]\n* Onions, chopped\n* 3 large [[Cookbook:Bell Pepper|bell peppers]], coarsely blended\n* 4–8 [[Cookbook:Habanero|habanero]] peppers (ata rodo), coarsely blended\n* 4–6 firm [[Cookbook:Tomato|tomatoes]]\n* ¼ cup [[Cookbook:Green Onion|spring onions]]\n\n==Procedure==\n# Cook the gizzard with salt, onions, beef seasoning, curry, and thyme. Add water, stir, and cook until soft.\n# Cook the beef with salt, onions, beef seasoning, curry, and thyme. Allow the beef to cook in its own juices, then add water and cook until soft.\n# Heat vegetable oil in a [[Cookbook:Frying Pan|pan]]. Add the cooked beef, and [[Cookbook:Searing|sear]] until golden brown. Remove from oil. Add the cooked gizzard to the hot oil, and [[Cookbook:Frying|fry]] until golden brown. Remove from oil.\n# Heat some oil in a [[Cookbook:Saucepan|saucepan]]. Add chopped onions, blended peppers, tomatoes, salt, stock cube, curry, and thyme. Fry for about 10–12 minutes.\n# Add the seared beef and gizzard and stir well. Stir in the spring onions, and [[Cookbook:Simmering|simmer]] for 2 minutes.\n# Remove from the heat, and serve.\n\n[[Category:Recipes using beef flank]]\n[[Category:Recipes using bell pepper]]\n[[Category:Recipes using curry powder]]\n[[Category:Recipes using salt]]\n[[Category:Recipes using thyme]]\n[[Category:Recipes using onion]]\n[[Category:Recipes using tomato]]\n\n[[Category:Recipes using dehydrated broth]]\n[[Category:Recipes using habanero]]\n[[Category:Recipes using vegetable oil]]","isRecipe":true,"recipe":{"name":"Beef and Gizzard Sauce","nameAr":null,"servings":null,"servingsSourceText":null,"ingredients":[{"id":"source-line-1","name":"1 kg chicken gizzard, washed","sourceText":"1 kg chicken gizzard, washed","amountText":"1 kg chicken gizzard, washed","amount":null,"unit":null,"foodBinding":null},